# Timeline conformance corpus.
#
# One entry per line: `<kind> <relative path>`.
#
# The corpus is enumerated here rather than discovered by walking directories,
# because directory iteration is unreliable in the WASM and Android emulator
# lanes this corpus exists to serve, and because an explicit index turns an
# unreferenced fixture into a visible omission rather than a silent one.
#
# Kinds — the corpus holds more than one shape of artifact, and nothing in the
# files themselves says which is which:
#
#   document  A complete `pulp.timeline.project` envelope, validated against a
#             sibling `<path>.expect` manifest on four axes: structural
#             summary, interchange concept census, the ordered identities of
#             every collection in the arrangement, and serialize idempotence.
#
#             The order axis is what makes the other three more than a
#             head count. Counts say how many survived; the identity orders say
#             which ones and in what sequence, so a dropped authored ordering or
#             a remapped identity is visible. Idempotence is deliberately not
#             one of those checks: it compares the pipeline against itself and
#             therefore cannot see an error both directions share.
#
#             Leaf content below a track — notes, automation points, MIDI lane
#             points, takes, comp segments — is still covered only by counts and
#             the census.
#   fragment  A single entity envelope (not a project), used for entity-level
#             migration tests. Declared so it is accounted for; entity-level
#             validation is not yet implemented, so it is reported as skipped
#             rather than silently ignored.
#   payload   A raw byte blob that is never parsed as timeline JSON — it is
#             embedded as OpaqueContent to prove unknown content round-trips
#             byte for byte. Deliberately never decoded.
#   ignore    Present in the tree but not part of this corpus — a foreign-format
#             interchange input, or a golden owned by a specific test. Listed so
#             the index stays exhaustive, which is what lets a completeness
#             check treat any unlisted file as an omission.
#
# Every entry is opened, including the kinds that are not validated: an entry
# reported as skipped but never touched would let a rename silently degrade the
# index into a comment while the run stayed green.
#
# Regenerate document manifests with:
#   pulp-fixture-runner --corpus <dir> --update
#
# A new schema version must add fixtures here. Keep entries grouped by version.

document v1/minimal.json
document v1/track.json
document v1/note-content.json
document v1/track-opaque.json
document v2/device-chain.json
document v2/midi-content-degenerate.json
document v3/automation-lane.json
document v3/clip-fade-shape.json
document v3/midi-content-lanes.json
document v4/sequence-markers.json
document v6/sequence-track-order.json
document v6/track-take-lanes.json

fragment v4/sequence-before-scenes.json

payload v1/unknown-content-envelope.json

ignore v1/replay-render.golden
ignore dawproject/linear_subset.dawproject.xml
ignore dawproject/out_of_subset.dawproject.xml
